WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.090
Disney's Encanto is full of hilarious, magical
moments, from Luisa and Isabela's amazing

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.940
songs to over-caffeinated kids and a sneaky
shapeshifting cousin.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.340
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm counting down the top 11 funniest

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.689
and most entertaining scenes in Encanto.

00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:19.740
Spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.419
Of the three main village kids who pop up
in the movie, caffeinated kid has the funniest

00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:26.419
moments.

00:00:26.419 --> 00:00:30.259
There's his feverish demand to know all the
family's powers during the opening song...

00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:32.349
Just tell us what everyone can do!

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:34.300
And that's why coffee's for grown-ups!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.390
And what about the way he still hangs on to
his coffee cup even when he's kicking a football?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.350
And how he revs himself up with caffeine to
help rebuild the Casita.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:47.820
Encanto co-director Jared Bush has revealed
his official name is "Pumped Juancho"

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:53.699
As well as being adorably amusing, the caffeinated
kid is also a nod to the Colombian custom

00:00:53.699 --> 00:00:56.219
of children drinking coffee.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:01:01.149
It's so comical during the first song how
Mirabel has to constantly dodge questions

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:03.179
from the kids about her own gift.

00:01:03.179 --> 00:01:07.500
And when they eventually find out she doesn't
have one, she's humorously brought crashing

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.970
back down to reality by a little girl.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.860
I am just as special as the rest of my family.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.900
All right, guys, where do I drop the wagon?

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.780
Maybe your Gift is being in denial.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.500
I made a rainbow!

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.140
Camilo's shape-shifting abilities provide
plenty of laughs...

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.850
Mirabel!
...including when he pretends to be his sister...

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:27.850
Camilo!

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.760
Stop pretending you're Dolores so you can
have seconds.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.190
Worth a shot.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.920
Ah!
...when he makes fun of Isabela by turning

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.630
into her suitor, and when he gets a shock
as Bruno and Mirabel race nosily through the

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:39.730
walls of the house.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:44.780
And, amusingly, when his shape-shifting gets
out of control, his head turns into a very

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.720
young child who sprouts an enormous moustache.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:53.340
Bruno, who's been living alone for years,
gets a heartbreakingly humorous moment with

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.980
his alter egos when Mirabel asks him if he's
been repairing the cracks in the house:

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.110
All the patching's done by Hernando.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.110
Who is Hernando?

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.490
I'm Hernando and I'm scared of nothing!

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:05.020
I used to say my real Gift was "acting."

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.030
I'm Jorge.

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.050
I make the spackle.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:12.540
By the way, "Jorge" pops up again briefly
during the finale as the Madrigals rebuild

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.140
their home.

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:18.700
And how absolutely adorable is the scene where
shy little Antonio gets his powers...

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.000
...and communicates with his new animal friends...

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Uh-huh.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.200
I understand you.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:28.500
...rides through his rainforest room on the
back of a jaguar, bounces about on a hammock,

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.240
and swings by on a snake!

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.830
And, frankly, let's face it, more movies could
benefit from adding capybaras!

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.120
There's some wonderful little details in this
scene too:

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.300
if you look carefully, you can see Dolores
put her hands over her ears as the crowd's

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.860
cheers become too much for her super-hearing.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.920
And what about the hilarious way that the
perfectly poised golden child Isabela swings

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.630
onto the scene as the family prepares for
Antonio's gift ceremony:

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.690
Did someone say flowers?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.690
Isabela!

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.030
Our angel!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.360
Please don't clap.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.920
Thank you.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.250
Oh, it's nothing.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:11.140
I love everything about this moment from the
way the murky scene changes to golden light

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:16.650
as Isabela works her magic, to the priceless
look on Mirabel's face as she watches her

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:22.670
effortlessly graceful sister swing by adored
by everyone there, to the serious Rapunzel

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:26.170
vibes I get from Isabela's magical swinging
vines.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:31.470
And to cap it all, Isabela literally throws
her gift in Mirabel's face!

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:36.209
The incredibly catchy Cha-cha style of "We
Don't Talk About Bruno" is an ingenious way

00:03:36.209 --> 00:03:40.490
to show everything Mirabel's estranged uncle
is blamed for in the family.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:45.240
I love Pepa and Félix's dance routine as
they explain how Bruno got inside her head

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:48.060
causing her to create a hurricane on their
wedding day.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.630
And the way Bruno's painted as a villain,
with Camilo shape-shifting and singing about

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:57.790
"rats upon his back", is darkly humorous;
then there's the townsfolk blaming him for

00:03:57.790 --> 00:04:02.790
their woes shows how everyone uses him as
a scapegoat for totally ordinary things that

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.430
can happen to anyone.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.430
And if you watch carefully, there's a fantastic
detail in the background, which some of our

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:13.810
eagle-eyed viewers spotted, as a hooded Bruno
bops along to the music behind Dolores and

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:14.830
Mirabel.

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:20.029
As the song ends, Dolores reveals she overheard
Bruno's vision of the magic dying and the

00:04:20.029 --> 00:04:25.680
house breaking apart, which leads into the
hilariously memorable dinner scene with Isabela's

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.800
suitor Mariano,

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.681
but just before we get to that, I want to
thank our video's sponsor HelloFresh who make

